## Commands

Use these exact forms — the flags keep output out of context.

```bash
[npm run dev]                              # dev server
[npm test -- --silent 2>&1 | tail -30]     # tests: trimmed output
[npm run build --silent]                   # build
[npm run lint -- --quiet]                  # lint
[npx tsc --noEmit 2>&1 | head -30]         # typecheck
```

## Output discipline

Command output persists in context and is re-read on every later turn in the
session. A single untrimmed log is paid for hundreds of times.

- Always trim: `| tail -30`, `| head -50`, `--silent`, `-q`, `--oneline`,
  `--tail=50`
- Large output → write to a file and grep it, don't pipe it through context:
  `[npm test] > /tmp/out.log 2>&1; grep -E "FAIL|Error" /tmp/out.log | head -40`
- Never `cat` a whole file to inspect it — use `sed -n 'START,ENDp'` or Read with
  an offset
- Never print a whole test run, build log, or `git log` when a slice answers the
  question
- Run genuinely noisy commands in a subagent and return only the conclusion

## Session hygiene

- One task per session. Tell me to `/clear` when a task finishes or I switch to
  unrelated work.
- Flag when context is getting large (~200K) and suggest `/compact` if we're
  mid-task, `/clear` if we're not.
- Never suggest changing model or effort mid-conversation — it invalidates the
  prompt cache and re-bills the whole context. Say "finish, `/clear`, restart on
  X" instead.
- Don't re-read files already read this session; don't re-run a command whose
  output is already above.

## Model expectations

Set before the session starts — this is a note for me, not something you change:

| Work | Model / effort |
| ---- | -------------- |
| Issues, PR text, docs, changelogs | Sonnet 5 / medium |
| Codebase search, mechanical refactors, test scaffolding | Sonnet 5 / low |
| Planning, implementation, debugging, review | Opus 5 / high |
| Never | Fable 5 |

If the current model clearly doesn't fit, say so in one line and continue anyway.

## Delegate read-heavy work

Use a subagent (Sonnet 5, low effort) for anything that means reading a lot to
answer a little — "find every call site of X", "which tests cover Y", sweeping
for a naming convention. Return the answer, not the file dumps.

